I left out both operations requests. Only the two code blocks below are part of the build. The node's other behaviour is unchanged.

- **Log file:** the build targets `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so the node has no filesystem to write to. `std::fs` calls would fail at runtime.
- **Metadata fetch:** the graph gives this node only `LLMClient<[lookup]>` and `DBHandle<'knowledge-base', read>`. Importing `aap:caps/http-client` would add authority the graph doesn't grant. It would also send the user's question text to an outside service, which the confined `conversation-context` boundary is meant to prevent.

If operations needs either, the right route is to add the capability to this node in the graph, such as an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` handle, or to have a host-tier node record inputs. The node body can then be regenerated against those interfaces.

The build error came from `AgentResponse`, `LlmError` and `Intent`. Only types named in the world's `use` are generated at the crate root, so these three are now imported from `crate::aap::caps::types`.

